+> - **Top-10 #2 (QuickSetTiers/QuickRank grid `FlatList`) — REFUTED, no fix
+>   needed.** The "default `flexGrow: 0`" premise below applies to plain
+>   `View`s, not ScrollView-derived components: RN's `ScrollView` base style
+>   (`baseVertical` in
+>   `react-native/Libraries/Components/ScrollView/ScrollView.js`) is
+>   `{flexGrow: 1, flexShrink: 1, overflow: 'scroll'}`, and a `style` prop
+>   merges *on top* of it. Both grids are direct children of a
+>   `flex: 1` chain (`SafeAreaView styles.safe` → `KeyboardAvoidingView
+>   styles.kav`), so a style-less `FlatList` is already bounded and scrolls
+>   internally at high chip counts. Verified against the RN source shipped in
+>   `mobile/node_modules` rather than the simulator — the base-style proof is
+>   stronger than an eyeball check. Same reasoning softens the
+>   RankImportSheet review-step concern: its explicit `{flexGrow: 0}` still
+>   inherits `flexShrink: 1` from the base style, so the list compresses into
+>   the capped sheet and scrolls rather than clipping.
+
